# Ruleset: Telemetry
#
# Expects a reject policy.
#
# Usage telemetry, product analytics, performance monitoring and crash reports. Hang this on a policy that can be switched off rather than a hard REJECT, so a suspected false positive is tested by flipping the policy.
#
# Scope: the ingestion host, never the vendor's dashboard or API, which keep their own file or FINAL. Feature flag and remote configuration hosts stay out, because a client that cannot fetch them changes behavior; so do push channels that share a vendor with its analytics. Our own services stay in Developer/Owned.list. A host whose company list sits in the overlay, ahead of the reject block (GitHub, AI, Tailscale coordination, the Apple pins), cannot be caught here.
#
# A host an app needs goes in source/protected.json, and the build fails if any reject list matches it.

# Developer tooling: wrangler, the Vercel CLI and Turborepo, Homebrew, 1Password, App Center, Tailscale's log service.
DOMAIN,analytics.brew.sh
DOMAIN,b5x-sentry.1passwordservices.com
DOMAIN,in.appcenter.ms
DOMAIN,log.tailscale.com
DOMAIN,sparrow.cloudflare.com
DOMAIN,telemetry.1passwordservices.com
DOMAIN,telemetry.vercel.com

